claimed: deploy-old-helm-retired -- one model, not two.

specs/deploy.md's `Deploy` and specs/deployment.md's `Deployment` have
been living side by side since stage 0, on purpose and temporarily.
okay-script currently commits TWO Helm charts and TWO compose files
for one application, which is exactly the drift this repository has a
rule against; the new model has now been proven on six targets and it
is time.

What the new model must gain first, because the old one carried it:

- the Dockerfile. It is not a target's file -- laptop, cluster and aws
  all reference the same image -- so it is rendered per module-run
  service into <moduleDir>/deploy/Dockerfile, where every target
  already points.
- Run.Module gains extraBuild and extraCopy (okay-demo links a Scala.js
  bundle in the build stage and copies it into the image).
- Service gains metricsPath, which the cluster target dropped and the
  old Helm chart had.

Then: okay-demo ports to a Deployment, okay-script drops its Deploy
value, and Deploy/Compose/Helm and the packaged chart resources go.
specs/deploy.md gets its supersession recorded rather than deleted.

Files: okay-deploy Deploy.scala + Deployment.scala + Cluster.scala +
resources, okay-demo DemoDeploy, okay-script ScriptDeploy, both
modules' committed deploy/ trees, tests, specs, boards.
